# Dedicated Playwright MCP browser

Browser automation should never silently attach to a daily browser containing live sessions.
Select an automation browser explicitly and install the build expected by the MCP package itself.

Example using Firefox:

```text
npx @playwright/mcp@latest install-browser firefox
claude mcp add playwright --scope user -- npx @playwright/mcp@latest --browser firefox
```

If an argument-free Playwright plugin is also enabled, disable it so it cannot register a second
server with different defaults. Do not edit a plugin cache because updates replace cached files.

Verification must cover behavior, not registration alone:

1. Invoke a browser navigation through the MCP.
2. Read the structured result and require its error field to be false.
3. Inspect the launched executable path while the browser is running.
4. Confirm the path belongs to the dedicated automation cache, not an installed daily browser.
5. Close the MCP and confirm its browser process exits.

The MCP can pin a different Playwright browser revision than the general `playwright` package.
Installing with `npx playwright install` may therefore download a browser the MCP will not use.
Use the MCP package's `install-browser` command.
